00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:05.110 align:start position:0%
hey this is presh talwalkar  i have found three consecutive integers  such that their product is equal to  their sum  what could my numbers be  solve for all possibilities  i received this problem by email and i  give credit to ken edwards for creating  this puzzle  can you figure it out  give this problem a try and when you're  ready keep watching the video for the  solution  let's suppose the middle number is x  then the three consecutive numbers would  be x minus one  x and x plus one  we need the product of these three  numbers to be equal to their sum  this means x minus one times x times the  quantity x plus one  needs to be equal to x minus one plus x  plus x plus one  we can simplify the sum  to be exactly three x  we can find the product slightly easier  if we multiply x minus one times x plus  one because this will lead to a  difference of squares  x squared minus one squared which is one  we then distribute the x and we get x  cubed minus x is equal to 3x  we now group the x terms on the left  hand side and we have the cubic equation  x cubed minus 4x is equal to 0.  we can then factor out the x  and then we have x times the quantity x  squared minus four  this is a difference of squares which we  can factor  as the quantities x plus two and x minus  two  we can now see there are three solutions  to this equation  x equals zero x equals negative two and  x equals two  each of these solutions will lead to a  triplet of numbers  we have  one case of minus one zero and one  we have another case of negative three  negative two negative one and we have a  final case of one two and three and  these are the only triplets of  consecutive integers in which their sum  is equal to the product  did you figure it out  thanks for watching this video please  subscribe to my channel i make videos on  math you can catch me on my blog mind  your decisions which you can follow on  facebook google plus and patreon you can  catch me on social media at  preshtalwalker and if you like this  video please check out my books there  are links in the video description
 

